# syscall-dispatch.manifest - syscalls that MUST have a live dispatcher
# case in kernel/proc/syscall.c. Enforced by
# tools/syscall-dispatch-gate/syscall-dispatch-gate, wired into the build
# via `make syscall-dispatch-gate` (an order-only prerequisite of
# kernel.elf, so it runs on EVERY build and a dropped case FAILS THE
# BUILD). Seeded from the full set of cases present at restore time; a
# dropped case (see #565/68199dd, which silently killed SYS_APP_VERIFY_SIG
# and the #563 signing-key split) is caught here, not in review.
#
# One SYS_* name per line. Add a name when you add a syscall case; remove
# a name ONLY when you deliberately retire the syscall, in the same change.
SYS_ACCEPT
SYS_ADDUSER
SYS_AI_SCAN
SYS_ALARM
SYS_APP_VERIFY_SIG
